<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Safety &amp; Compliance</p>
    <h1>Safe handling. Clean storage. Honest disposal.</h1>
    <p class="lead">The same bottle protects a crop or harms a family — the difference is practice. These are the non-negotiables for every AGREXA product user.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" style="padding-top:44px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div class="card" style="border-top:5px solid var(--leaf)">
        <h3>🧤 Before you spray — PPE minimums</h3>
        <ul class="check-list" style="margin-top:14px">
          <li>Full-sleeve cotton shirt + full trousers (no shorts, no bare arms)</li>
          <li>N95-style mask or clean cotton face cover for wettable powders</li>
          <li>Nitrile rubber gloves — never bare hands for mixing</li>
          <li>Closed shoes/boots; change socks immediately if wet</li>
          <li>Goggles when mixing dusts or SKY-toxic herbicides like paraquat</li>
          <li>Spray against no wind above 10–12 km/h; never into the wind</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="border-top:5px solid var(--soil)">
        <h3>🧴 Mixing rules</h3>
        <ul class="check-list" style="margin-top:14px">
          <li>Use a measuring cup supplied or graduated beaker — no bottle-cap guessing</li>
          <li>Dissolve SP/SG powders in a separate bucket first, then add to tank</li>
          <li>Never mix unfamiliar products — jar-test with a small volume first</li>
          <li>Never mix with 'copper' products a reactive tank-mate without checking compatibles</li>
          <li>Tank order: wettable powders → flowables → EC solutions; spray within 2 hours of mixing</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="border-top:5px solid var(--amber)">
        <h3>🏚 Storage that saves lives</h3>
        <ul class="check-list" style="margin-top:14px">
          <li>Locked room, away from kitchen, feed, seed and drinking water</li>
          <li>Off the floor on wooden pallets; ventilated, not next to a stove</li>
          <li>Original label intact — never store in soft-drink or oil bottles</li>
          <li>Keep the SDS sheet of each product stapled to the row shelf</li>
          <li>Log book: batch number, opening date, remaining quantity</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="border-top:5px solid #8C2F1F">
        <h3>🗑 Disposal — after the spray</h3>
        <ul class="check-list" style="margin-top:14px">
          <li>Rinse empty containers 3× (rinse-water goes into the spray tank)</li>
          <li>Puncture and crush triple-rinsed containers; hand to dealer or CSC centre</li>
          <li>Never burn containers near homes or release rinse into ponds</li>
          <li>Wash spray clothing separately from family laundry</li>
          <li>Shower immediately after spraying; wash before eating/drinking</li>
          <li>Old/expired stock: give it to the dealer for scientific disposal, never pour in the field</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<hr class="furrow">

<section class="section tint">
  <div class="wrap split" style="align-items:start">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Environment &amp; residue</span>
      <h2>Keep the residue off your plate</h2>
      <p class="lead">A pre-harvest interval (PHI) is the legally fixed gap between last spray and harvest. It is the single most important food-safety number on the label.</p>
      <div class="pf-cards" style="margin-top:18px">
        <div class="pf-block"><h4><span class="dot"></span>PHI 7 days</h4><p>Early vegetative-stage protects like Mancozeb on many crops — check label, crop by crop.</p></div>
        <div class="pf-block"><h4><span class="dot"></span>PHI 14 days</h4><p>Most insecticides (Cartap, Emamectin, Imidacloprid labels differ by crop)</p></div>
        <div class="pf-block"><h4><span class="dot"></span>PHI 21 days</h4><p>Grain-filling systemic fungicides like Tebuconazole on groundnut</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:16px">For mango/chilli export-grade production, prefer the bio line (neem, Bt, Trichoderma) inside 30 days to harvest.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <h3>Government regulations &amp; links</h3>
      <ul class="check-list" style="margin-top:14px">
        <li><a href="https://cibrc.nic.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CIB&amp;RC — Central Insecticides Board (label claims &amp; registrations)</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://ppqs.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Directorate of Plant Protection — quarantine &amp; storage rules</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://agri.telangana.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Telangana Dept. of Agriculture — farmer schemes</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://agricoop.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ministry of Agriculture &amp; Farmers Welfare</a></li>
        <li>FSSAI MRL standards for harvested produce</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="booking-note" style="margin-top:12px">Buying or selling unregistered pesticides is an offence under the Insecticides Act 1968.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="callout" style="border-left:6px solid var(--amber)">
      <h3>First aid — print this and stick it on the store wall</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-3" style="margin-top:16px">
        <p><b>Skin contact:</b> remove clothing, wash area with soap + water 15 min. No scrubbing.</p>
        <p><b>Eyes:</b> flushed with clean water 15 minutes, seek a doctor if irritation lasts.</p>
        <p><b>If swallowed (conscious):</b> drink water, induce nothing; carry the product label to the hospital immediately. <b>Paraquat: no gastric delay — go to hospital instantly.</b></p>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:14px">National Poison Helpline — AIIMS: <a href="tel:1800116117"><b>1800 116 117</b></a> · AGREXA support: <a href="tel:+919014791483"><b>90147 91483</b></a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

